  "clinical_uncertainties": [],
  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "All right, Dana, the booking note says insulin review, and then in brackets, lows at night. Is that the headline?",
      "start_timestamp": "00:00",
      "end_timestamp": "00:09",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "That's the headline. Okay, so, you know I got that new sensor in the fall? The one that beeps? It woke my husband up before it woke me, which tells you something about how deeply I sleep through my own lows.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:12",
      "end_timestamp": "00:31",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "About twice a week. Usually around three in the morning. I wake up drenched, my pajamas are soaked, and I have to go eat jelly beans in the dark like a raccoon.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:42",
      "end_timestamp": "00:59",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Mostly real. The sensor says fifty-something, and my finger stick agrees, within a few points. Last Tuesday it said forty-four, and I just sat on the kitchen floor eating a banana, honestly feeling kind of silly.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:13",
      "end_timestamp": "01:31",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I'm wiped out in the afternoons. Like around two, three o'clock I hit a wall. I thought it was the lows messing with my sleep, but maybe it's something else.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:41",
      "end_timestamp": "01:58",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Could be both. Let me ask about some other things. Any blurry vision lately?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:01",
      "end_timestamp": "02:08",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, my eyes are fine, I had my eye exam last month, and they gave me the thumbs up.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:09",
      "end_timestamp": "02:19",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Numbness or tingling in your feet?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:20",
      "end_timestamp": "02:24",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, nothing like that. My feet are the one part of me that behaves.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:25",
      "end_timestamp": "02:34",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And any vomiting or stomach upset, because that can throw the sugars off.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:35",
      "end_timestamp": "02:42",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Nope, no vomiting. Stomach's been good. Which is a relief, since I'm not allowed gluten anyway, so I'm cautious.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:44",
      "end_timestamp": "02:53",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "So at bedtime, I take glargine, 20 units. Then with meals I take lispro, usually about 6 units, depending on what I'm eating and what the sensor says. And then lisinopril, 5 mg every morning, for the blood pressure.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:08",
      "end_timestamp": "03:28",
      "supports": [
        "medications[1]",
        "medications[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And your other conditions, I have type 1 diabetes of course, high blood pressure, and celiac disease. Anything else?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:29",
      "end_timestamp": "03:40",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "That's the list. Oh, and my appendix came out when I was fifteen. It's in my chart somewhere, I think. Does that count?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:41",
      "end_timestamp": "03:53",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[2]",
        "medical_history.surgical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I run three mornings a week, about five miles. And on Saturdays I have the 5K group, which is more of a social hour with some jogging.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:07",
      "end_timestamp": "04:21",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Exactly. Okay, let me get your numbers. Arm out, please. Blood pressure is 122 over 76.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:06",
      "end_timestamp": "05:15",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Pulse is 70, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, temperature 36.7, and you weigh 176 pounds on our scale.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:27",
      "end_timestamp": "05:38",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[1]",
        "vital_signs[2]",
        "vital_signs[3]",
        "vital_signs[4]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Those are all good. Here's what I think. The overnight lows look most likely like too much of the long-acting insulin at bedtime, particularly after exercise.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:48",
      "end_timestamp": "06:01",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "A small step, not a big one. I'd like you to cut the glargine from 20 units down to 18 units at bedtime, and keep everything else the same.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:20",
      "end_timestamp": "06:35",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Then text the clinic, and we'll adjust again by another two. Meanwhile, have a small snack at bedtime on the days after you run.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:45",
      "end_timestamp": "06:56",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I also want a fresh HbA1c blood test before I see you, so we can see the longer picture.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:08",
      "end_timestamp": "07:20",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Perfect. And I'd like to see you in three months to review how the nights are going.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:32",
      "end_timestamp": "07:40",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[3]",
